    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d222">

                <pb facs="0498" n="472" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v09/pg472"/>

                <head>222. Telegram From the Embassy in Japan to the
                        Consulate General in Geneva<anchor n="0"
                        xml:id="d222-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Tokyo</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1961-07-12T12:00:00+09:00">July 12, 1961,
                            noon</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>10. From Ball. Geneva for John Evans,
                    information to Department for Martin. Deeply concerned about state Dillon Round
                    negotiations due to meagerness US offers. I feel it is essential this situation
                    be brought to attention of the President, including indication extent to which
                    limited character of our offers stems from peril point proposal.</p>
                <pb facs="0499" n="473" xml:id="pg473"/>
                <p>Suggest you prepare draft memorandum from Secretary to President which would set
                    forth in simple terms danger extensive withdrawal by EEC and UK of offers tentatively
                    made, in view inadequacies US offers; consequences such restrictive action for
                    free world economy; impact minimal results Dillon Round on US exports, etc.</p>
                <p>I will want to discuss general problem with Wyndham-White immediately upon my
                    arrival Geneva and then go over draft memorandum with you.</p>
                <p>After transmittal this draft memorandum to Washington I want Martin and Schaetzel to put it in final form, with
                    particular reference steps which might be recommended to President to improve US
                    offers in order to avoid downward spiraling of Dillon Round negotiations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Reischauer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
